# Toggle tabs.
#
# The same idea as an ordinary tab to a person, and the opposite of one in the DOM. A tab panel gives
# every tab its own element-name, so each tab is an element and 'click' switches it. A toggle group
# has one element-name for the whole group and names the tabs inside it only by their captions, so
# the group is the element and the open tab is its value.
#
# That is why these lines use 'set' and 'check-value' rather than 'click': no new command was needed,
# only a new element type.

use Supervisor
open UsrTestForm for 71d27c81-3d6b-41d9-9a39-c408c96173b6

# The group lives on this tab, and Creatio reopens a page on the tab it was last left on.
click TabContainer_qtw0r0n

check ButtonToggleGroup_dqmg1ty exists

set ButtonToggleGroup_dqmg1ty "Tab 2"
check-value ButtonToggleGroup_dqmg1ty eq "Tab 2"

set ButtonToggleGroup_dqmg1ty "Tab 1"
check-value ButtonToggleGroup_dqmg1ty eq "Tab 1"

# The Feed/Attachments toggle Creatio puts on every page is the same kind of control, so it is
# addressed the same way and needed no configuration of its own beyond analysis.
#
# Creatio marks a tab as selected only after it has been clicked, so a freshly opened group reports
# no open tab at all and the first switch cannot be asserted. Switching twice makes the second one a
# real change whichever tab the group started on.
check CardButtonToggleGroup exists
set CardButtonToggleGroup "Attachments"

set CardButtonToggleGroup "Feed"
check-value CardButtonToggleGroup eq "Feed"

# Left on the tab the rest of the suite expects to find the page on.
click GeneralInfoTab
